      "findings": [
        "H_t is defined as past states, controls and measurements, so the current control u_t is not explicitly included in its conditioning information. The intended o3 transition equality requires that current input. In a valid controlled Markov example x_t=u_t with independent binary u_t and a fixed past, p(x_t=1|past)=1/2 but p(x_t=1|x_(t-1),u_t=1)=1. Define H_t=(x_0:t-1,z_1:t-1,u_1:t), or put u_t on the left as well. The supplied explanation states the intended dependence but does not repair the missing left-side conditioning premise. Source p1384 explicitly includes u_1:t."
      ]
